        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1690">

                <pb facs="1379" n="1263" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 319.112 R 15/128.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 97.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 23, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your instruction No. 34, of February 19th last, relative to [etc.].
                    According to your directions I laid the facts of this matter before Señor
                    Chiari, Minister for Foreign Affairs, in the sense of your instruction, also
                    handing to him an aide mémoire embodying the substance of my verbal
                    communication. * * *</p>
                <p>On the 13th instant I received a note dated the 12th instant, a copy and
                    translation of which are enclosed. * * *</p>
                <p>Señor Chiarí has since informed me verbally that the policeman No. 667 serving at
                    Bocas del Toro under the name of Balbino Palma has been ascertained to be
                    Indalecio Franco and has accordingly also been dismissed. Señor Chiarí further
                    stated that to prevent any further reinstatement of these men, their photographs
                    had been taken and sent to all the police stations in the Republic.</p>
                <p>I have thought well to have Señor Chiari’s statements confirmed by, the Zone
                    Police who now inform me that it is a fact that these three men have been
                    dismissed and duly photographed. I have accordingly verbally stated to Señor
                    Chiari my appreciation of his Government’s disavowal and expressions of regret
                    and of its prompt action.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Percivical Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1690-a1.xml" xpointer="d1690-a1"/>
